## `bus/RingBufferEventBus.java`
A simple low-overhead implementation using a fixed ring buffer and a single consumer.
```java
package com.example.trading.bus;

import com.example.trading.common.Event;

import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;

public final class RingBufferEventBus implements EventBus {
    private final Event[] ring;
    private final int mask;
    private final AtomicLong writeSeq = new AtomicLong(0);
    private volatile EventHandler handler;

    public RingBufferEventBus(int powerOfTwoSize) {
        if (Integer.bitCount(powerOfTwoSize) != 1) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Size must be power of two");
        }
        this.ring = new Event[powerOfTwoSize];
        this.mask = powerOfTwoSize - 1;
    }

    @Override
    public void publish(Event event) {
        long seq = writeSeq.getAndIncrement();
        ring[(int) seq & mask] = event;
        EventHandler h = handler;
        if (h != null) {
            h.onEvent(event);
        }
    }

    @Override
    public void subscribe(EventHandler handler) {
        this.handler = handler;
    }
}
```

