## Better latency monitoring

For real monitoring, add a histogram. Here’s a tiny fixed-bucket example:

```go
type LatencyHistogram struct {
	Buckets [16]uint64 // buckets in powers of 2 microseconds
}

func (h *LatencyHistogram) Record(d time.Duration) {
	us := uint64(d.Microseconds())
	b := 0
	for us > 0 && b < len(h.Buckets)-1 {
		us >>= 1
		b++
	}
	atomic.AddUint64(&h.Buckets[b], 1)
}
```

This gives you a cheap distribution without high overhead.

