# Performance Improvements for Next Iteration

To make this genuinely ultra-low-latency:

## 1. Replace linear rule scan
Instead of checking every rule:
- Use hash tables for exact matches
- Use prefix trie for IP ranges
- Separate rule paths by protocol

## 2. Batch classification
- Parse the packet once
- Use SIMD-friendly access patterns
- Separate fast path and slow path

## 3. Per-core worker model
- One RX queue per core
- One TX queue per output port
- Avoid locks entirely

## 4. Precompiled rules
- Convert rules into lookup tables at load time
- Build decision DAGs

## 5. Cache-aware memory layout
- Use struct-of-arrays for hot fields
- Align data to cache lines

## 6. RSS / flow steering
- Let NIC distribute flows by hash
- Keep packets of a flow on the same core

