## 7) Minimal engine integration pattern

At the engine side, you typically:

1. Create an instance of the plugin.
2. Initialize it during startup.
3. On each frame:
   - read engine transforms into physics bodies if needed
   - call `Tick(dt)`
   - write physics transforms back to engine objects
4. Shutdown cleanly.

Pseudo-code:

```cpp
CustomPhysics::PhysicsPlugin Physics;

void OnEngineStart()
{
    Physics.Initialize();

    auto world = Physics.GetWorld();
    auto body = world->CreateBody(CustomPhysics::BodyType::Dynamic, {});
    body->SetMass(10.0f);
}

void OnEngineUpdate(float deltaTime)
{
    Physics.Tick(deltaTime);

    // Sync body transforms back to engine actors here
}

void OnEngineShutdown()
{
    Physics.Shutdown();
}
